llm_response:
The login/logout control is contained within the `userlinks` block of the browsable API's base template. When you override the template by extending `rest_framework/base.html` and define your own blocks, you are replacing the default content of those blocks.

To ensure the login/logout links survive your customization, you must use `{{ block.super }}` within the `userlinks` block in your custom template. This preserves the default authentication links while allowing you to add your own links alongside them.

Your custom template should look like this:

```html
{% extends "rest_framework/base.html" %}

{% block userlinks %}
    {{ block.super }}
    <!-- Add your custom links here -->
{% endblock %}
```

The `userlinks` block is specifically defined as a list of links on the right of the header that, by default, contains the login/logout links. Using `{{ block.super }}` is the recommended way to add links instead of replacing the existing ones.

